## Add extra content to the flyout

To add extra flyout content, add an HTML element to the page and give it a 
```
facetwp-flyout-tpl
```

 class. It will automatically get hidden with CSS.

Within this element, add a 
```
{content}
```

 placeholder to automatically output the facets. Then add additional content above or below this placeholder. This content can be text, HTML, or shortcode(s).

Here’s a full example:

```
<!--Add this HTML to your page-->
<div class="facetwp-flyout-tpl">
  This text/HTML/shortcode appears above the facets.
  {content}
  This text/HTML/shortcode appears below the facets.
</div>
```

Warning:**Don’t add any facets to the flyout this way**, as that will lead to JavaScript errors. The only facet type you can add this way is the User Selections facet, [as shown below](#add-user-selections-to-the-flyout). To change the facets displayed in the flyout, or change their order, you can [use the “facetwp/flyout/facets” filter hook](#customize-the-facets-and-facet-order-in-the-flyout).

### Add User Selections to the flyout

You can use shortcodes within the 
```
facetwp-flyout-tpl
```

 HTML block. For example, if you want to show the [User Selections](/help-center/facets/facet-types/user-selections/) above the other facets in the flyout, place this HTML block somewhere on the page. It will automatically get hidden with CSS:

```
<!--Add this HTML to your page-->
<div class="facetwp-flyout-tpl">
  [facetwp selections="true"]
  {content}
</div>
```

Warning:**Don’t add any other facet types to the flyout this way**, as that will lead to JavaScript errors. The only facet type you can add this way is the User Selections facet, as shown above. To change the facets displayed in the flyout, or change their order, you can [use the “facetwp/flyout/facets” filter hook](#customize-the-facets-and-facet-order-in-the-flyout).

### Add a Submit or Apply button to the flyout

If you are using the [Submit button add-on](/help-center/add-on-features-and-extras/submit-button/) to redirect facets to another results page, and you want the Submit button to appear at the bottom of the Flyout, you can add the button HTML like this:

```
<!--Add this HTML to your page-->
<div class="facetwp-flyout-tpl">
  {content}
  <button class="fwp-submit" data-href="/listings/">Submit</button>
</div>
```

Or, if you are [using an Apply/Submit button to refresh](/how-to-disable-facet-auto-refresh-and-add-an-apply-button/), you can add the button HTML like this:

```
<!--Add this HTML to your page-->
<div class="facetwp-flyout-tpl">
  {content}
  <button onclick="FWP.refresh()">Apply</button>
</div>
```

