## Format Date Range facet selections in the User Selections facet

If you have a Date Range facet and a [User Selections facet](/help-center/facets/facet-types/user-selections/) on the page, you’ll notice that Date Range selections in the User Selections facet are not formatted according to the [date format](#date-formatting) set in the [“Display format” setting](#display-format).

We may be adding a fix in a future update. Until then, you can add the following snippet to your (child) theme’s functions.php to let the date format also work for User Selections:

```
How to use custom PHP code?PHP code can be added to your (child) theme's functions.php file. Alternatively, you can use the Custom Hooks add-on, or a code snippets plugin. More infoadd_action( 'facetwp_scripts', function() {
  ?>
  <script>
    (function($) {
      if ('object' !== typeof FWP) {
        return;
      }

      FWP.hooks.addFilter('facetwp/selections/date_range', function(output, params) {
        var $el = params.el;

        let min_input = $el.nodes[0].querySelector('.facetwp-date-min');
        let max_input = $el.nodes[0].querySelector('.facetwp-date-max');
        let min_formatted = min_input && min_input._altInput ? min_input._altInput.value : null;
        let max_formatted = max_input && max_input._altInput ? max_input._altInput.value : null;

        params.selected_values = params.selected_values.map(function(dateval, index) {
          if (!dateval) return dateval;
          let formatted = (index === 0) ? min_formatted : max_formatted;
          return formatted || dateval; // fall back to original value if no formatted version
        });

        return output;
      }, 1); // Let it run before the same hook is used by FacetWP to parse the dates for User Selections

    })(fUtil);
  </script>
  <?php
}, 100 );
```

The above works for **every** Date Range facet. If you want this to work only for a **specific** Date Range facet, you can do it as follows. Replace the 
```
my_daterange_facet
```

 with the name of your Date Range facet, in [line 14](#date-range-user-selections-format-facet-L14).

```
How to use custom PHP code?PHP code can be added to your (child) theme's functions.php file. Alternatively, you can use the Custom Hooks add-on, or a code snippets plugin. More infoadd_action( 'facetwp_scripts', function() {
