### Legacy ways of customizing the marker cluster icons

There are a few [legacy ways of customizing the marker cluster icons](/help-center/facets/facet-types/map-legacy/advanced-map-customizations-legacy/customize-marker-clustering-legacy/#customize-the-marker-cluster-images) that we made backward compatible with the current marker clusterer implementation. With “legacy” we mean the situation **before** FacetWP v4.4 with the Map add-on v2.0.

These legacy methods all use the 
```
facetwp_map_init_args
```

 PHP hook. The advantage of using this PHP hook is that the needed code is a lot shorter than doing it in the new JavaScript way, [using a custom renderer](#customize-the-marker-cluster-icons-with-a-custom-renderer).

#### Method 1: Using imagePath and imageExtension

![The default five 'legacy' PNG marker cluster icons.](https://facetwp.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/markerclusters-with-clustericons.jpg)The default five “legacy” PNG marker cluster icons.
To create five marker cluster icons based on the number of contained markers, with your own icons, use the following code.

The five cluster icons’ sizes and colors represent the number of markers in the cluster. Which of the five cluster icons is shown, is calculated based on the number of markers in that specific cluster. From the smallest to the largest icon, the conditions to show that icon are: 
```
<10
```

, 
```
<100
```

, 
```
<1000
```

, 
```
<10000
```

, and 
```
>=10000
```

 markers.

[Option 1](#map-init-args-imagePath-imageExtension-L4-L5) uses the five “legacy” cluster icons that are available within the Map add-on files. The backward compatibility uses the legacy logic and icon colors/sizes [as noted below](#map-init-args-imagesizes). So this basically restores the old situation (before v2.0 of the Map add-on), as shown in the image on the right.

[Option 2](#map-init-args-imagePath-imageExtension-L7-L8) shows how to use your own icons instead. For this to work, you need to make a custom directory in your theme. In this example, this directory would be 
```
/assets/img/googlemaps
```

. The 
```
