 hook filters the [facet selection choice HTML](#customize-html-output-L23), for **each individual selection** of **each facet** in the User Selections.

This hook can be used to change the HTML of the selection choice, which is passed in the hook’s  
```
selection_choice
```

 [parameter](#facet-selection-choice-html-L12).

The hook has access to the facet name of the facet selection choice HTML it filters, with its 
```
facet_name
```

 [parameter](#facet-selection-choice-html-L12). You could use this to only customize the facet selection choice HTML for specific facets.

The following example wraps each individual selection choice in a 
```
<li></li>
```

 container, except the selection choice of the 
```
my_sort_facet
```

 facet. This would be helpful make the selection choices wrap on smaller-width devices, if combined with the removal of the 
```
<li></li>
```

 container around the facet selection HTML (containing the facet label + facet choices), [using the facetwp/selections/facet_selection_html hook](#facet-selection-html). See [the section below](#style-individual-selections-as-single-wrapping-items) for a full example.

```
